e_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fresh and unguessable per construction; answers two questions producerId alone cannot \u2014 is this a retransmit or a restarted producer, and did this acknowledgment come from a real delivery. A consumer keyed on producerId alone would absorb the whole post-restart prefix as duplicates and still ack them as delivered."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_producer_controller_retransmission", "label": "Retransmission with the same seq", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/producer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_producer_controller_confirm_callback", "label": "confirm callback on send", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/producer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "reliable-delivery.send is fire-and-forget with no ask-based acknowledgment, so pacing sends against confirmations is the only way to turn queueing into real backpressure."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_producer_controller_in_memory_buffer", "label": "In-memory unacked buffer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/producer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_producer_controller_one_to_one_link", "label": "One ProducerController per ConsumerController", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/producer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_producer_controller_producercontroller", "target": "docs_sr